# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.7: the payload is a
# module or a guest built with the NBT toolchain, run by NBT Manager's
# nbt-runner (runner); the native form's lines are in native.args.
# It draws on the manager's surface (show) and is used with the iDrive
# controller; a USB gamepad, the status line and live settings when granted.
--app
hello-lvgl
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.7
--bridge-uses
show,controller,runner
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,gamepad
# Settings: key|Label|default|choices. At most 12; src/ui.cpp reads them,
# tests/test_hello_lvgl.py checks they are declared.
--setting
theme|Theme|dark|dark,light
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install (NBT Manager's PROTOCOL.md,
# "Package information").
--property
Project|NBTFoundry examples
--property
Licence|MPL-2.0; LVGL MIT; fonts OFL-1.1
--text
A dial and a button made of LVGL widgets: an example of an LVGL application on NBT Manager.
--text=
--text
Do not interact with it while driving.
--text=
--text
Source, licences and notices: https://github.com/NBTFoundry/examples
